    "final_stop_contract_verdict": "No concrete violation under that lifecycle.\n\n`stop` sets `stopping` before `shield` and leaves it set if the waiting caller is cancelled. `shield` lets the current turn finish. The `finally` clears the handle only when that same task is already done, so a cancelled waiter keeps the live worker.\n\n`start` returns while that worker exists, before recovery, new locks, `stopping = False`, or a new task. Queued rows stay queued. Only a later `start`, after the old worker has exited and the handle is cleared, clears `stopping` and runs the next job once.",
